-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  suite_cli_help_editor.adam - `adam help editor` (no banner): editor's
  usage (any number of files), its summary (the editor started on its own,
  adam back at once, pcpp's), the options every command takes and its
  example, exit 0. Nothing here starts the editor
*******************************************************************************/

/*
@@test
  kind cli
  targets x86_64-windows-gnu
  args "--no-banner" "help" "editor"
  exitcode 0
  | USAGE:
  |   adam editor [<file> ...] [options]
  |
  | Start the Adam editor on its own, with each <file> open; adam returns at once
  |
  | OPTIONS:
  |   --no-banner  Print no banner: for scripts and tests
  |   -q, --quiet  Print only the reports: no banner, no phase or status lines (scripts, tests)
  |   -h, --help   Show the help of the command given (else adam's)
  |
  | EXAMPLES:
  |   adam editor hello.adam
@@end
*/

module exe suite_cli_help_editor;

begin
end.
